     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). That makes this about twice the maximum.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg. Doses that high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily or about 567 mg three times daily. This is a common way to reach 1,700 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at some frequency.\n\nIf you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
