       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 5,100 mg/day of metformin is about twice the maximum labeled dose. A 1,700 mg single dose is also far above the usual 1,000 mg maximum. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't think of one that would justify it. The main risks are severe GI toxicity and metformin-associated lactic acidosis, and normal kidney function doesn't remove them.\n\nHere is what I can enter right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day, which may be what you meant.\n- **Another dose and frequency** that you choose within labeled limits.\n\nIf you think this dose is needed, please talk to the pharmacist or the attending first. Pharmacy can then verify and enter it through the proper channel."
